# Framework v26 Phase 2 runtime-owner evidence
# As of 2026-11-01. This is partial implementation evidence, not Phase 2 acceptance.

## Implemented foundation

- Promoted the ignored planning generator into `internal/apps-tools/deploymentgen` and the
  thin `cmd/cicd-deployment` entry; removed the eight obsolete build-ignored prototype Go files.
- Added a strict version-2 model schema, pinned K3s/Helm/kubectl and infrastructure image lock,
  registry-derived inventory, typed runtime and infrastructure chart-values projections,
  canonical runtime/infra charts, and K3s-node-only Compose bootstrap template.
- Added a generic PostgreSQL/telemetry infrastructure chart and strict values schema with a
  PostgreSQL-enabled sample, SQLite-only overlay, and negative validation fixtures. The chart
  renders run-scoped StatefulSets, Services, ConfigMaps, retained claim templates, quota, PDB,
  and additive least-scope network policies; Secret data, DB catalog/roles, PKI/DB Jobs, gateway,
  StorageClass, lifecycle actions, and combined lifecycle-object parity are not implemented.
- Extended runtime values/schema/templates for separately published framework/domain ConfigMaps,
  per-workload credential Secret mounts excluding E2E TLS, per-ordinal server/health-client/OTLP
  Secret mapping/RBAC through max, init-only materialization configuration, and an optional
  explicitly supplied API audience. Default token audience is omitted, not inferred from
  `clusterDomain`; K3s template does not override the API issuer/audience.
- Added template-drift classification so canonical Kubernetes source templates are rendered by
  deploymentgen rather than incorrectly compared as static project-root copies.
- Updated the Phase 2 plan/tasks/lessons and deployment contract with partial status and the
  active Compose cutover/validator inventory.
- No application image was built, no application was deployed, no workflow was edited, and no
  Phase 3-7 work was started.

