## Blocked gates and root cause

- Full normal/tagged builds, shuffled repository tests, and deployment matrix validation have not
  been rerun after these changes.
- Baseline commit hooks initially found test `goconst` findings and UTF-8/LF/editorconfig drift;
  those source issues were corrected. A later hook run passed `lint-fitness`, but
  `golangci-lint` typechecking failed while writing Go work files under `R:\Go\GOTMP` with
  “There is not enough space on the disk.” The focused package test and lint later passed; the
  full hooks have not been rerun, so that prior capacity failure remains unresolved for checkpoint
  purposes.
- Main's read-only investigation measures the fixed `R:` volume at 8 GiB with approximately
  3.7 MiB free and found no large abandoned Go build directories under `GOTMP`/`OSTMP`. After
  the focused test/lint run, a local read-only measurement showed 112.43 MiB free. The
  prior listing of `R:\Go\GOTMP\TestTelemetryInitializers_ApplyMTLSCredentials1785621155\001`
  contains `ca.crt` (570 bytes), `client.crt` (542 bytes), and `client.key` (241 bytes). No
  certificate contents were inspected and no cache or temp data was removed.
- Main measured `GOCACHE` file lengths totaling 6,426,931,500 bytes and `MOD_CACHE` file lengths
  totaling 1,506,695,524 bytes. Host `C:` has abundant free space, but inherited cache/temp paths
  remain unchanged; no cache was cleared, storage resized, or shared setting reconfigured.
- `GOCACHE`, `GOTMPDIR`, `TMP`, `TEMP`, Docker allocations, and user caches were not changed or
  cleared. No `--no-verify` or hook bypass was used. No commit was made; the clean checkpoint
  still requires full hooks/builds to pass and a clean worktree.
- Main has since supplied an owned Linux validator image/container with Go 1.27.3, pre-commit
  4.6.2, golangci-lint 2.14, 4 CPU/6 GiB and fresh owned Linux storage. The framework worker
  owns the broad Go-validation slot; focused deploymentgen tests and Helm integration checks have
  been run there, but runtime-owned broad gates remain pending serialized scheduling. No host
  cache/temp settings or shared storage were changed.

