## 2026-11-01: Explicit chart-values CLI extension

- Added production CLI modes `runtime-values` and `infrastructure-values`. Runtime values require
  an exact single-release selector and explicit non-secret JSON input; the input and projected
  output are validated against canonical schemas. The input supplies digest-pinned images,
  resources, backend-specific arguments/configuration, and storage values rather than relying on
  invented defaults. Infrastructure values project the complete inventory using canonical infra
  defaults; partial infrastructure preview is read-only.
- `-write` and `-check` for runtime values target
  `deployments/k8s/generated/<run>/<helm-release>/values.yaml`; infrastructure values target
  `deployments/k8s/generated/<run>/infra/values.yaml`. The command entry creates parent
  directories for generated outputs. Values are JSON, which is YAML-compatible; no cluster
  operations occur.
- Focused PASS in the owned Linux validator after the CLI edits:
  `go test -shuffle=on -count=1 ./internal/apps-tools/deploymentgen
  ./internal/apps-tools/cicd_deployment` (1.540s and 0.011s respectively).
  Earlier targeted checks also passed the strict input-schema/decoder test, chart projection helper
  across every release, the CLI preview/write/check/failure matrix, and generated-directory writer.
- These are focused current-source checks only. The production binary has not yet been rebuilt
  after the latest Go edits; broad normal/tagged builds, full shuffled suite, coverage, linters,
  deployment/fitness validators, configured hooks, CLI-driven Helm render, and clean checkpoint
